#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Friendly little cli client that can do most everything microbin supports
# right from your terminal.
#
# Two modes:
#
#   list mode (default)  GET /list, unauthenticated. Deletion uses
#                        GET /remove/{key} and is restricted to entries that
#                        expose a Remove link, matching the behaviour of the
#                        page itself.
#
#   admin mode (-a)      POST /admin/ with multipart username and password
#                        fields, as submitted by the /auth_admin form. The
#                        returned table carries size, encryption, private and
#                        editable flags and hit counts. Deletion uses the action link
#                        present in each row, falling back to the path given by
#                        --delete-path (default /delete). This applies to every
#                        entry, including those with no Remove link on /list.
#
# Sizes in list mode are obtained with a one-byte Range request rather than
# HEAD: file routes are registered as #[get] only, so HEAD falls through to the
# 404 handler. The Content-Range and Content-Disposition headers of the 206
# response supply the total length and the original filename.
#
# Standard library only.

